x=by['cex-abelian-variety-does-not-have-good-model-over-every-base'];s=x['statement'];s=s[:s.index('This contradicts the general principle')]+'''This contradiction proves the asserted absence of an abelian scheme model. For the hypothetical model, properness identifies A[2](K) with A[2](R), while finite etale lifting identifies the latter with A[2](k). The special fibre has dimension one and its two-torsion has four geometric points by the multiplication theorem. The valuation equality 3v(x)=v(t)=1 proves directly that x^3+t has no root in k((t)); Eisenstein is an alternative, not a needed supplier. The example's explicit ramified extension shows that good reduction need not descend through that ramified extension.''';setx(x['id'],s,x['deps']+['thm-valuative-criterion-properness'])
